      "id": 1,
      "text": "Garvin began as Terry, named for Union General Alfred Terry, before the railroad renamed it in 1881 after a railroad official.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garvin%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s streets were laid out as First, Sherman, Grant, and Sheridan, reflecting Civil War heroes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://lakesnwoods.com/GarvinHistory.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The station was first called Terry for about a year before becoming Kent, then finally Garvin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
